-- title:
--   Recognising a place through a K-homomorphism via a separating test family
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $F$, $E$ be fields with $F$ and $E$ algebras over $K$, and suppose there is $x \in F$ with $F$ finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$. Let $\varphi : F \to E$ be a $K$-algebra homomorphism, let $s$ be a place of $F/K$ and $w$ a place of $E/K$ — that is, valuation subrings $\mathcal O_s \subseteq F$, $\mathcal O_w \subseteq E$ containing the image of $K$, different from the whole field, and principal ideal rings — and let $T \subseteq F$ be a set of test elements subject to four conditions: (hT) $\varphi(t) \in \mathcal O_w$ for every $t \in T$; (hvan) for all $t \in T$ and $c \in K$, if $t - c$ lies in the nonunits of $\mathcal O_s$ then $\varphi(t) - c$ lies in the nonunits of $\mathcal O_w$; (hO) some $t \in T$ and $c \in K$ satisfy $t - c \in \operatorname{nonunits}(\mathcal O_s)$ with $t \neq c$ in $F$; and (hsep) $s$ is the only place $s'$ of $F/K$ with $T \subseteq \mathcal O_{s'}$ and with $t - c \in \operatorname{nonunits}(\mathcal O_{s'})$ whenever $t \in T$, $c \in K$ and $t - c \in \operatorname{nonunits}(\mathcal O_s)$. Then for every $g \in F$ one has $g \in \mathcal O_s$ if and only if $\varphi(g) \in \mathcal O_w$; here elements of $K$ are understood through the structure maps $K \to F$, $K \to E$.
--
--   This is the transport statement saying that, under the stated separation conditions, the valuation ring of $w$ pulls back along $\varphi$ exactly to the valuation ring of $s$, so that $w$ lies over $s$; the test family $T$ together with the values of its members at $s$ determines $s$ among all places of $F/K$. It is used in the modular-curve layer, where places of function fields of modular curves are identified through explicit ring homomorphisms, for instance in the results on reading off branch places and on descent along the Igusa ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_mem_toValuationSubring_iff_map_mem_of_forall_place_eq_of_testFamily.lean

